# Registers the AI provider selectors.
#
# ChatProviderEnvironmentPostProcessor decides whether the chat model comes from Groq or from
# local Ollama, based on whether GROQ_API_KEY is set. EmbeddingProviderEnvironmentPostProcessor
# does the same for embeddings, on GEMINI_API_KEY: Gemini when it is set, local Ollama when it is
# not. Both have to run as environment post-processors because Spring AI gates each provider's
# model autoconfiguration on a selector property that is matchIfMissing = true, so an unset
# selector means every provider on the classpath tries to define the bean — and only one may
# exist. A YAML placeholder cannot express "use this one only when a key is present".
#
# The key is org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor — the spring.factories entry
# Spring Boot 4 itself uses for the built-in post-processors.
org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.nocteon.nocteon_api.ai.config.ChatProviderEnvironmentPostProcessor,\
com.nocteon.nocteon_api.ai.config.EmbeddingProviderEnvironmentPostProcessor